+# TASK-260830-8x76g1 logbook (RUN-260901-885c85)
+
+- The provisioned story worktree already contained the revision 14 candidate, including work newer than both recovery archives. Restoring either archive over it would have discarded reviewed work, so the archives were verified and treated as recovery inputs only.
+- CR revision 14 requested a test-only correction. Production `closed_shapes.go` stayed byte-for-byte unchanged.
+- Exact-error negative tests were added at both public identity entries for every reviewer-named live refusal clause. The submodule case-collision proof uses a narrowing mutation (`EqualFold -> ==`), not merely clause deletion.
+- A full 110-site refusal deletion sweep exposed helper-level gaps beyond the twelve named rows. Recursive member deletion, registry-nil, helper-type, and subsumption tests were added without changing production behavior.
+- The exact-current refusal sweep result is 85 killed and 25 raw survivors, with zero actionable survivors after explicit reachability/subsumption triage. The rev12 numeric sweep is 56 killed and 15 raw survivors, also zero actionable.
+- `task-board validate` exited 0 but emitted 262 inherited `MISSING_ACTIVITY` diagnostics for other board items. This task was not named in those diagnostics; the result is recorded as a successful command with non-clean inherited board output, not as a clean board.
