+# TASK-260830-8x76g1 developer evidence (RUN-260901-885c85)
+
+## Outcome
+
+This test-only review rework closes the twelve refusal gaps reported by CR revision 14. The public production flow remains:
+
+`CalculateObjectIdentity` / `VerifyObjectIdentity` -> `prepareObjectIdentity` -> `validateImmutableObjectShape` -> the schema-specific closed-shape validator.
+
+`internal/canonicaljson/closed_shapes.go` was not changed. Its SHA-256 remains `3d34cb52cb483e513a8ba398ed351993a02c46c01d5f4086af083f038304b307`.
+
+Changed task scope:
+
+- Added `internal/canonicaljson/clause_refusal_test.go`.
+- Updated `internal/canonicaljson/testdata/constraint-enumeration.md` so claimed cross-field and member-presence evidence names the executable public-entry tests.
+
+The tests drive both public identity entries and pin exact refusal reasons for invalid `env_literals` keys, Board Identity logical IDs and local URL nullability, WorkspaceSnapshot subject equality, Git ref/tagged-union rules, submodule case collisions and initialized-state invariants, pack/features format equality, and symlink/hardlink target types. A recursive deletion test walks every member of all 24 registered closed shapes represented by eight valid fixture families. A registry guard test proves that a registered schema cannot silently resolve to a nil validator.
+
+This identity operation does not mutate durable state, so crash/idempotency recovery evidence is not applicable.
+
+## Mutation evidence
+
+| Sweep | Corpus | Killed | Raw survivors | Actionable survivors | Evidence |
+| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | --- |
+| Refusal-clause deletion | 110 sites | 85 | 25 | 0 | `clause-sweep/final-results.tsv`, followed by exact-current rerun `final-survivor-rerun.tsv` |
+| Numeric/boundary rev12 generator | 71 mutants | 56 | 15 | 0 | `TASK-260830-8x76g1-review14/final-derived-results.tsv` |
+| Case-collision narrowing | 1 mutant | 1 | 0 | 0 | `clause-sweep/narrowing-result.txt` |
+| Special widening/bypass attacks | 5 mutants | 5 | 0 | 0 | `clause-sweep/special-widening-results.txt` |
+
+The narrowing mutation `strings.EqualFold(pathValue, previous) -> pathValue == previous` exited `go test` with code 1 and failed `TestSpecDerivedRefusalClausesReachBothIdentityEntries/submodule_sibling_path_case_collision`, proving the case-collision rule by narrowing rather than deletion. The attached mutation triage accounts for every raw survivor.
+
+## Direct validation results
+
+Every command below was run as a standalone foreground command. No result was piped through `tee`.
+
+| Command | Exit code | Result |
+| --- | ---: | --- |
+| `test -z "$(gofmt -l internal/canonicaljson/clause_refusal_test.go)"` | 0 | formatted |
+| `go build ./...` | 0 | pass |
+| `go vet ./...` | 0 | pass |
+| `go test ./... -count=1 -v` | 0 | pass, including new public-entry negative cases |
+| focused five-test canonicaljson refusal/member/registry selection | 0 | pass on the exact handoff tree; 624 verbose output lines |
+| `go test ./... -race -count=1` | 0 | pass |
+| `go test ./... -cover -count=1` | 0 | pass; canonicaljson statement coverage 87.1% |
